## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design cross-cloud, per-tenant data pipelines with strong semantics and security for fintech data.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming ingestion with Pub/Sub and Dataflow
- BigQuery exactly-once semantics via insertId; tenant isolation via datasets
- Snowflake ingestion via Snowpipe from GCS
- CMEK, IAM scoping, retries, DLQ, schema evolution

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pub/Sub message -> JSON parse and enrich (pseudo-beam-like)
function parseMessage(msg){
  const obj = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(msg.data, 'base64').toString());
  obj.ingest_ts = Date.now();
  return obj;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency across both targets?
- What changes if Snowflake needs micro-batch loading instead of Snowpipe?
- How would you monitor latency and cost at scale?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests event-driven design, Cloud Run vs Cloud Functions, and idempotent outputs in GCS pipelines. It also covers IAM least privilege and basic testing strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Storage finalize events
- Cloud Functions and Cloud Run integration
- Idempotent object writes in GCS
- IAM bindings for service accounts
- Containerized image processing with ImageMagick or similar

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cloud Function (node) skeleton
exports.thumbsTrigger = async (data) => {
  const bucket = data.bucket;
  const name = data.name;
  // call Cloud Run with metadata
  await fetch(RUN_ENDPOINT, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ bucket, name })});
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test locally and with CI for this flow?
- How would you handle transient failures and retries without duplicating work?

